invariant: INV-48
file: src/mlkem.c
catches: test/mlkem-builds.sh
reason: the AVX2 copy's modulus check is guarded on a macro no build
  defines, so a session with CH_CPU_AVX2 reads an ek's fields one group
  at a time. Nothing else objects: the loop refuses the same keys, and
  only the time is wrong. The script requires the copy for x86-64 to call
  mlk_field_at_or_above_q_avx2.

--- old
#ifdef CH_MLKEM_AVX2_COPY
    return mlk_field_at_or_above_q_avx2(ek, t_bytes);
--- new
#ifdef CH_MLKEM_AVX2_COPY_PATH
    return mlk_field_at_or_above_q_avx2(ek, t_bytes);
